B.push(P(`**Timing quality is not trivial.** That the score rewards timing does not make every timing mechanism equally good. The health-indicator threshold alarm, which times its alarm on a classical linear health indicator, placed ${f1(Math.min(...ctrlDS.map(d => CT[d]['20'].HI_threshold.pct)))}–${f1(Math.max(...ctrlDS.map(d => CT[d]['20'].HI_threshold.pct)))}% of first warnings in the window, significantly fewer than the recipe on each of the seven datasets after Holm's correction (largest adjusted *p* = ${fmtp(Math.max(...ctrlDS.map(d => CT[d]['20'].HI_threshold.p_holm)))}, N-CMAPSS), with many alarms too early (${R2.window.PHM08['20'].HI_threshold.early} of ${R2.window.PHM08['20'].HI_threshold.n} on PHM08). A fairer indicator-based opponent maps the same indicator to cycles to failure and uses the recipe's own trigger and selection rule. On PHM08 and FD001–FD004 this calibrated indicator placed ${f1(Math.min(...HC5.map(d => HC[d]['20'].pct)))}–${f1(Math.max(...HC5.map(d => HC[d]['20'].pct)))}% of first warnings in the window, close to the uncalibrated alarm and significantly fewer than the recipe on each (largest Holm-adjusted *p* ${fmtp(Math.max(...HC5.map(d => HC[d]['20'].vs_recipe.p_holm)))}). On N-CMAPSS it placed ${f1(HC.NCMAPSS6['20'].pct)}%, against ${f1(CT.NCMAPSS6['20'].STW.pct)}% for the recipe (${HC.NCMAPSS6['20'].vs_recipe.only_a} against ${HC.NCMAPSS6['20'].vs_recipe.only_b} discordant engines, Holm-adjusted *p* = ${fmtp(HC.NCMAPSS6['20'].vs_recipe.p_holm)}) and ${f1(CT.NCMAPSS6['20'].HI_threshold.pct)}% for the uncalibrated alarm. By the interpretation fixed before this analysis, on PHM08 and FD001–FD004 the gradient-boosted regressor contributes timing information that a linear indicator expressed in cycles does not, whereas on N-CMAPSS, where the recipe itself was weak, calibration in cycles accounts for the recipe's timing. The regressor's value therefore lies in when its trajectory crosses the level, which the window score rewards, rather than in the number it reports at the crossing, which the score barely uses. Under an identical protocol on PHM08 the recipe scored significantly higher than re-implemented LSTM, similarity and convolutional approaches, and not significantly differently from a multilayer perceptron with a Kalman filter that shares its features or from a hybrid Transformer given its inputs (Supplementary Section S15), so it is a reasonable instrument for this analysis, not a claim about the best model.`));
